;; The skills shipped in the binary, in listing order. An index, because a
;; built binary cannot list a resource directory (as agents/index.edn is).
;; An entry is a skill's name — resources/brainyard/skills/<name>/SKILL.md —
;; or {:name "<name>" :resources ["file" …]} naming files under its
;; resources/ that calling it hands over too. No scripts: an embedded file is
;; not on disk for bash to run (RFC-017).
;; A project shadows one by name: .brainyard/skills/<name>/ replaces it.
["skill-authoring"]
